course: dictionary
lesson: 13169
title: Fourteenth: position and parts
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fourteenth is an ordinal number. It tells you the position of something in a line or list, like first, second and third. If thirteen children are in front of you, you are the fourteenth. «Maya was the fourteenth child to reach the finish line.» Thirteen children got there before her.
explain: Fourteenth is written 14th. The 14 is the number, and the th shows it is a position in order. Fourteenth is not the same as fourteen: «Fourteen children» is a count, but «the fourteenth child» is a place in the line.
explain: A fourteenth can also be a part of something. It means one of 14 equal parts, written 1/14. «She cut the pizza into fourteen equal slices and ate one fourteenth.» Check the words around it: when it is a part, there is usually «a» or «one» in front, and the thing is shared out equally.
fact: Fourteenth means number 14 in order.
fact: 14th is the short way to write fourteenth.
fact: A fourteenth is one of 14 equal parts of something, and it is written 1/14.
fact: «My fourteenth birthday» means the birthday when you turned 14.
fact: Fourteenth goes in the same list as first, second, third and so on, and it often comes after thirteenth.
exercise: «Ravi came fourteenth in the race.» What place did Ravi come? | Fortieth | *Fourteenth | Fourth | Fourteen
exercise: «She ate a fourteenth of the cake.» What does a fourteenth mean here? | *One of 14 equal parts | Fourteen whole cakes | Half of the cake | The fourteenth cake in the shop
exercise: «It was my fourteenth birthday last week.» What does fourteenth tell us? | A party with fourteen guests | *The birthday when I turned 14 | A birthday that lasted fourteen days | A birthday with 14 cakes
test: Thirteen children stand in front of Ana in a line. What place is Ana in? | Fourth | *Fourteenth | Fifteenth | Thirteenth
test: Which fraction means one fourteenth? | *1/14 | 1/4 | 1/41 | 14/1
exam: Which word means position 14 in a line of 20 children? | Thirteenth | Twelfth | *Fourteenth | Fifteenth
